  48:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  *
  49:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * SYNC message is used for synchronization of the nodes on network. One node can be SYNC producer,
  50:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * consumers. Synchronous TPDOs are transmitted after the CANopen SYNC message. Synchronous receive
  51:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * accepted(copied to OD) immediatelly after the reception of the next SYNC message.
  52:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  *
  53:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * ####Contents of SYNC message
  54:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * By default SYNC message has no data. If _Synchronous counter overflow value_ from Object diction
  55:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * different than 0, SYNC message has one data byte: _counter_ incremented by 1 with every SYNC tra
  56:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  *
  57:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * ####SYNC in CANopenNode
  58:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * According to CANopen, synchronous RPDOs must be processed after reception of the next sync messs
  59:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * there is a double receive buffer for each synchronous RPDO. At the moment, when SYNC is received
  60:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * internal variable CANrxToggle toggles. That variable is then used by synchronous RPDO to determi
  61:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  * buffers is used for RPDO reception and which for RPDO processing.
  62:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h ****  */
  63:CANopen/301/CO_SYNC.h **** 
